(* Negative control neither-none: the session handshake over TLS 1.3 with no pin and no binding, against an attacker that
   holds no key at all (AUD-5, #389). This is the middlebox of ADR-0023 that terminates the TLS session of the client with
   a certificate of its own and opens a session to the server: the two Noise handshakes cross it unchanged, and it reads
   and rewrites every record. With either protection alone it needs a key (nobinding-cert, nopin-noise); with neither it
   needs none. *)

process
  ( Setup()
  | Sessions(pin_off, bt_none, plabel_session, lab_exp_session, suite_hfs)
  )
